-- title:
--   Base change of the Z-chart of a projective Weierstrass model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$, and let $K$ be a commutative ring with an $R$-algebra structure. For a projective Weierstrass curve $V$ over a base, write $\mathrm{ProjModelRingCR}\,V$ for the quotient of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by $V$'s defining cubic, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules under the quotient map (`projModelGradingCR`). Let $\psi$ be the graded ring homomorphism from this graded ring for $W.\mathrm{toProjective}$ to the one for $(W.\mathrm{map}\ (\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ K)).\mathrm{toProjective}$ induced by coefficientwise extension of scalars $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]\to K[X_0,X_1,X_2]$; this is well defined because the extension carries the ideal generated by the cubic of $W$ into that generated by the cubic of its base change, and it respects the gradings. Let $z$ denote the class of $X_2$. The assertion is that the square of affine schemes consisting of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `Away.map ψ z` (the map of degree-zero homogeneous localisations away from $z$), the two structure morphisms of these $D_+(z)$-chart rings to $\mathrm{Spec}\,K$ and $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$ respectively (given by $K$, resp. $R$, mapping into the degree-zero part and thence into the localisation), and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ K$, is a pullback square of schemes.
--
--   This records that the $D_+(Z)$ affine chart of the projective Weierstrass model commutes with base change: the chart ring of the base-changed model is $K \otimes_R$ the chart ring over $R$. It is one of the three chart cases assembled in [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_awayIsPushoutAll`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_awayIsPushoutAll), which expresses the projective model of a base-changed Weierstrass curve as a fibre product over the base.
